        "code": {
          "text": "Upper respiratory symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Symptoms for approximately 5 days: scratchy throat initially, now nasal congestion and rhinorrhoea, mild dry cough, and feeling a bit washed out."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated symptoms and home temperature"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Afebrile at home; eating and drinking okay. Denies shortness of breath, chest pain, wheeze, facial pain, purulent sputum, and gastrointestinal symptoms."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Additional reported symptoms denied"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies haemoptysis, confusion, ear pain, ear discharge, sinus tenderness, severe headache, photophobia, and neck stiffness."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Possible symptom triggers"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient queried whether symptoms may have been triggered by new scented washing powder or air conditioning at shops."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Patient-reported hearing change"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports hearing has 'gone down another notch' and that the TV is louder; husband has complained. Hearing feels worse and more blocked during the current head cold when the nose is congested."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated hearing symptoms denied"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies unilateral symptoms, sudden hearing loss, vertigo, new tinnitus, ear fullness, and otalgia."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Bedside hearing assessment"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Conversational voice heard at 1–2 m with hearing aids in; occasional repetition needed, especially with corridor noise. Whisper test was less reliable due to anxiety and background noise. Overall picture described as consistent with known bilateral sensorineural hearing loss, with no obvious asymmetry."
      }
    },
    {
